# Day 6 – Feature Engineering

**Date:** *7 July 2026*

## Objectives

To understand the importance of Feature Engineering and learn techniques for transforming existing data into meaningful features suitable for further analysis and model development.

## Session Overview

The session focused on **Feature Engineering** as an important part of data preparation. We learned how existing features can be modified or combined to improve data representation and help models identify useful patterns.

The major techniques covered included **Feature Creation, Transformation, Scaling, Encoding, Binning, Feature Extraction, and Feature Combination**. We also discussed methods such as standardization, normalization, and converting categorical values into numerical form.

## Key Takeaways

- Understood the role of Feature Engineering in data preparation.
- Learned how to create and transform meaningful features.
- Explored numerical feature scaling and categorical encoding.
- Understood binning, feature extraction, and feature combination.
- Learned how well-designed features can improve data representation and model performance.

## Learning & Implementation

Practiced different Feature Engineering techniques using **Python and Pandas**. Worked with numerical and categorical features, explored feature transformations and scaling methods, and created derived features to make the dataset more informative for future model development.

## Project Progress

Applied Feature Engineering concepts to the project dataset by exploring existing features and identifying opportunities to create more meaningful ones. Practiced feature transformation, scaling, encoding, and feature creation to improve the dataset's representation for upcoming model development.

