# Day 7 – Principal Component Analysis (PCA)

**Date:** *8 July 2026*

## Objectives

To understand dimensionality reduction and learn how PCA can reduce the number of features while preserving important information in a dataset.

## Session Overview

The session introduced **Principal Component Analysis (PCA)** as a dimensionality reduction technique for handling high-dimensional data. We learned how PCA transforms existing features into new **Principal Components** based on the variance present in the data.

The session also covered **feature scaling, explained variance ratio, principal components, and PCA visualization**. We discussed how reducing unnecessary dimensions can simplify data analysis and improve computational efficiency.

## Key Takeaways

- Understood the need for dimensionality reduction.
- Learned how PCA creates new principal components.
- Understood the role of variance and explained variance ratio.
- Learned why feature scaling is important before PCA.
- Explored visualization of reduced-dimensional data.

## Learning & Implementation

Practiced the PCA workflow on sample data, including feature scaling, dimensionality reduction, and visualization of principal components.

## Project Progress

Explored PCA in the context of the project dataset and identified how dimensionality reduction could be useful when dealing with multiple related features. Practiced the basic PCA workflow to understand its possible application in the project.
