# Day 8 – Handling Class Imbalance

**Date:** *9 July 2026*

## Objectives

To understand class imbalance, its effect on model predictions, and different techniques used to create a more balanced dataset.

## Session Overview

The session focused on **Class Imbalance**, where one target class has significantly more observations than another. We learned how imbalance can lead to biased model predictions, particularly toward the majority class.

The session covered **target distribution analysis, encoding, stratified train-test splitting, oversampling, undersampling, SMOTE, Tomek Links, ADASYN, and combined resampling techniques**.

## Key Takeaways

- Understood the problem and impact of class imbalance.
- Learned how to identify and visualize class distributions.
- Understood the purpose of stratified data splitting.
- Explored oversampling and undersampling techniques.
- Learned different approaches such as SMOTE, ADASYN, and Tomek Links.

## Learning & Implementation

Practiced different class-balancing techniques on sample datasets and compared how resampling methods change the distribution of minority and majority classes.

## Project Progress

Analyzed the target-class distribution of the project dataset to understand the presence of class imbalance. Explored suitable balancing techniques that can be considered before model training.
