# Day 10 – Automated Data Profiling & EDA Tools

**Date:** *13 July 2026*

## Objectives

To explore automated EDA and data profiling tools that provide quick and detailed insights into dataset structure, quality, distributions, and relationships.

## Session Overview

The session focused on automating parts of **Exploratory Data Analysis** using Python-based tools. We explored **YData Profiling** for generating detailed reports containing statistics, missing values, distributions, correlations, and duplicate information.

We also learned about **Sweetviz** for interactive visualization and dataset comparison, along with **D-Tale** for browser-based exploration, filtering, sorting, and analysis of datasets.

## Key Takeaways

- Understood the purpose of automated EDA tools.
- Learned how YData Profiling generates comprehensive reports.
- Explored Sweetviz for visualization and dataset comparison.
- Learned how D-Tale supports interactive data exploration.
- Understood how automated tools can make dataset analysis faster.

## Learning & Implementation

Created and explored automated profiling reports using different EDA tools. Compared their capabilities for understanding dataset quality, feature distributions, correlations, and relationships.

## Project Progress

Applied automated EDA tools to the project dataset to obtain a broader view of its structure and quality. Generated profiling and visualization reports to identify useful patterns and areas requiring further analysis.



